WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.396 --> 00:00:02.576
Wow! Who are you?

2
00:00:02.596 --> 00:00:03.617
I am a peacock.

3
00:00:03.637 --> 00:00:04.777
We are large birds.

4
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.538
Where do you live?

5
00:00:09.618 --> 00:00:13.539
We live in India, Indonesia, and Africa.

6
00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:35.145
We live in forests and sleep in trees.

7
00:00:36.866 --> 00:00:37.927
What do you eat?

8
00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:41.028
We look for food on the ground.

9
00:00:42.749 --> 00:00:45.170
We like berries, seeds, and flowers.

10
00:00:47.251 --> 00:00:49.132
Your tail is colorful!

11
00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:53.154
Males have long feathers with eyespots.

12
00:00:55.295 --> 00:00:57.716
We spread our feathers to show them off.

13
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.341
That helps us find mates.

14
00:01:05.883 --> 00:01:08.945
Do female peacocks have colorful feathers too?

15
00:01:10.206 --> 00:01:13.168
Females are called peahens, not peacocks.

16
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.231
Some have brown feathers.

17
00:01:17.792 --> 00:01:20.534
But others have colorful feathers like males.

18
00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:24.096
Do you have any enemies?

19
00:01:25.998 --> 00:01:28.580
Big cats and stray dogs hunt us.

20
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.981
Some animals eat our eggs.

21
00:01:33.542 --> 00:01:36.223
People love our feathers and hunt us too!

22
00:01:38.444 --> 00:01:39.765
Do peacocks sing?

23
00:01:39.785 --> 00:01:44.567
No. We make loud sounds to find mates.

24
00:01:46.088 --> 00:01:48.809
When we spot danger, we make noise too.

25
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.190
That warns everyone in the forest!

26
00:01:54.311 --> 00:01:55.152
I hear others.

27
00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:00.006
I'm going to show off my feathers.

28
00:02:00.026 --> 00:02:03.715
Good-bye, Peacock!
